2026-09-27T10:32:34.8250249Z Update Note
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8250688Z ===========
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8251253Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8251807Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8252005Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8252455Z ================
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8252764Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8253077Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8254465Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8254867Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8255106Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8255704Z ====================================
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8256025Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8256358Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8257125Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8257888Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8259156Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8260168Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8260480Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8261349Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8262348Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8262914Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8263828Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8264619Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8264800Z Packages
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8265235Z ========
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8265496Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8267803Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8269256Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8269544Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8270178Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8271104Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8271803Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8272491Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8273045Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8273695Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8273885Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8274230Z ==========================
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8274407Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8276061Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8277299Z 
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8277998Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8278996Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T10:32:34.8279279Z 
